__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.run.lock
.pytest_cache/
logs/
.vscode/

# Generated outputs. Every one of these is rendered from data/history.db on
# each run, so a committed copy is stale the next day -- and worse, a checkout
# silently restores the stale copy over fresh output. That is how dashboard.html
# came to show Costco at $947.74 (its 2026-08-21 price) a month later.
/dashboard.html
/history.html
/reports/*.html

# The day's raw capture. history.db is the store these feed; keeping a handful
# of arbitrary days in git backed nothing up and made `--no-fetch` render from
# a month-old snapshot as though it were current. With none present that path
# fails loudly instead, which is the better failure.
/data/fundamentals_*.csv.gz
/data/estimates_*.csv.gz
/data/holdings_*.csv.gz
/data/insiders_*.csv.gz
.DS_Store

